  "details": "Something that would be extremely useful is the ability to use group roles to manage an instances ability for people to join. \n\nA common scenario currently is getting a group event ready with staff, then portaling to a new world with the full instance information available. \n\nYou could do an example with three roles. Owner, Staff, attendees. Initial world creation and only owner is able to join. Then that owner is able to set the rules for the instance and say hey I want staff to be able to join. So then staff joins and then after they have their spots, then the owner allows attendees to join. \n\nHowever, what I would like is to be able to edit the permissions for the world for who can join. I would like to be able to say hey staff can join, but nobody else. But once we have staff there to be able to mark, okay everyone is okay to join now. Or just another role is available to join.\n\nBeing able to dynamically change the permissions for who can join an instance in a group instance would be a massive benefit to those who use groups.",
